UMT SiswaPost Smart Parcel Collection System (SPACS) facilitates the process of handling parcels on campus from arrival to collection. First, user profiles and access control are managed by Admins and users Students, Staff and Admins log in securely with their UMT credentials. Staff scan the barcode when the parcel arrives, and match it to a student's account automatically and allocate it to a shelf or locker. The system then creates a unique QR code and PIN which will be released to the student, with automatic reminders if the package is overdue. Lastly, Staff can check the code to leave a digital log of delivery when picked up, and Students are able to track their deliveries on a real-time dashboard and Admins can generate daily or monthly delivery reports.
